<title>UK: Reckitt off as SBC Warburg downgrades.</title>
<headline>Reckitt off as SBC Warburg downgrades.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Reckitt &amp; Colman Plc fell on Tuesday, defying strength elsewhere in the UK market, as analysts at SBC Warburg cut the stock to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot; on valuation grounds, dealers said.</p>
<p>Reckitt shares -- which shot to a record 997p on Monday -- were down 5p at 980-1/2 by 0851 GMT in modest volume of 790,245 shares.</p>
<p>Analysts at the investment bank could not immediately be reached for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
